    lsm:documentation "A data type of String SHOULD identify a data point that is either a text value consisting of a word, phrase, sentence, paragraph, or formatted (TAB, CR, LF) character content depending on its purpose or a numeric value with a maximum of 16383 characters and MAY have the lang attribute. There is no list of valid values provided. EXAMPLE: A Disqualificaton Reason Text for excluding a product from those offered to a borrower could be expressed as \"Does not meet income to indebtedness guidelines for down payment support.\"." ;
